---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";

const lastUpdated = "August 18, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Safety"
  description="How Covey handles safety expectations, reports, and urgent concerns."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-[var(--section-y)]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Safety</div>
    <h1 class="display t-h1 mb-4">Safety at Covey</h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-ink-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] mb-12">
      Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <div class="card p-6 mb-12">
      <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        Covey is built for people making plans in the real world. Use care when
        meeting someone, choose public places when appropriate, and report
        behavior that makes the community less safe.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Community expectations</h2>
        <p>
          Treat people with respect. Do not harass, threaten, discriminate,
          impersonate others, share private information without consent, spam
          people, or use Covey to coordinate illegal or dangerous activity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Reporting concerns</h2>
        <p>
          If something in the app feels unsafe, report it from the product when
          available or email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.safety}`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">
            {SITE.emails.safety}
          </a>.
          Include the account, plan, message, or screenshot context that would
          help us understand what happened.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">What Covey may do</h2>
        <p>
          We may review reports, restrict content or visibility, warn users,
          suspend accounts, preserve evidence, or contact support providers when
          needed to investigate abuse, fraud, security issues, or policy
          violations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Emergencies</h2>
        <p>
          Covey support is not an emergency service. If you or someone else is
          in immediate danger, contact local emergency services first. For
          non-emergency help with an account or plan, contact support at
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.support}`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">
            {SITE.emails.support}
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
